\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Let the song go round the earth:
\par Jesus Christ is Lord,
\par Sound His praises, tell His worth,
\par Be His name adored;
\par Every clime and every tongue
\par Join the grand, the glorious song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Let the song go round the earth,
\par From the eastern sea,
\par Where the daylight has its birth,
\par Glad, and bright, and free;
\par China's millions join the strains,
\par Waft them on to India's plains.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Let the song go round the earth,
\par Lands where Islam's sway
\par Darkly broods o'er home and hearth, 
\par Cast their bonds away;
\par Let His praise from Afric's shore
\par Rise and swell her wide lands o'er.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let the song go round the earth:
\par Where the summer smiles,
\par Let the notes of holy mirth
\par Break from distant isles;
\par Inland forests, dark and dim,
\par Snow- bound coasts give back the hymn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Let the song go round the earth:
\par Jesus Christ is King,
\par With the story of His worth,
\par Let the whole world ring,
\par Him creation all adore
\par Evermore and evermore.  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

